cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BPFCompat in research, please cite the software using this metadata."
title: "BPFCompat: empirical eBPF compatibility testing across real Linux kernels"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Arı"
    given-names: "Eren"
    alias: "ErenAri"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kernel-Guard/bpfcompat"
url: "https://github.com/Kernel-Guard/bpfcompat"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  BPFCompat is an open-source compatibility validator for compiled eBPF
  artifacts. It boots real Linux distribution kernels in disposable virtual
  machines, executes libbpf or project-specific loader paths, and records
  structured load/attach evidence so compatibility is measured empirically
  rather than inferred only from kernel versions or CO-RE assumptions.
keywords:
  - eBPF
  - BPF
  - Linux kernel
  - compatibility
  - kernel testing
  - libbpf
  - systems research
